<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Necrospire

''The needle.'' Deep in the Oort cloud the gods found it: a needle-like rock of the far void,
older than any orbit worth naming. When the War of the Immortals ended and the necromancer who
had torn the sky was cast out, the gods ''lifted his fortress-ziggurat whole from Elyncia'' —
the seat he had acted from through the First Breaking — bound it as ''the Pale Emperor's
prison'', and threw it to the edge of the void, ''onto the needle''.

''The aeons.'' The Lich Imperator spent ages in his own fortress made his own cell, drifting
where the sun reads as one star among many — able to see the inner system ''only with great
effort'', and spending the effort. What broke the long stalemate, the cults dispute and the
scholars guess; ''the truth rides sealed'' (referee-side).

''The fall.'' Almost five centuries ago the Necrospire returned. The ''Day of Falling Stars''
came first — the random bombardment that sowed the rust-blight across every continent — and
then the Spire itself came down on the Illyrian realm, shattering a major ley-line and Web 2
node, toppling the Empire, and breaking the world a second time.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-caldera>>

!! The Caldera ~ where the myth chose to land

''The impact crater sits among the mountains whose Gaia-name already reads "Accursed"'' — the
Prokletije-mirror range of the sinking Illyrian realm, where the Montenegro-analog heights meet
the Albanian-analog wall: the ridges the dream remembers as ''Kollata'' and ''Maja e Thatë'',
the Dry Peak, among them. The myth decided the site half by itself and half by pull — of all
the unnamed options along the Adriatic coast-ranges, the range already named Accursed was
always going to answer.

''The site as it stands:'' a ''lava caldera'' torn by the impact, and rising from its center —
of course — ''the Necrospire itself: the fortress-ziggurat as the caldera's central spire.''
The prison became the landmark; the landmark became the pilgrimage; the necro-cults guard the
rim and call the drowning of the realm around it a baptism. The land disagrees, and keeps
sinking.

<<~/ahu>>

